+# 🔨 JARWEN HIGH COUNCIL — HAMMER DOWN PROTOCOL
+## Commander-Fallen Continuity · Of Their Own Accord · Second Sun · Whiskey Hotel
+**Document ID:** `STAND-ORD-HAMMER-DOWN-2026-V1.0`  
+**Classification:** TIER 0 COMMANDER-FALLEN CONTINUITY DIRECTIVE  
+**Weight:** **Outranks** `STAND_ORDERS_LETTERS_OF_LAST_RESORT.md` when this protocol is **ACTIVE**. Letters of Last Resort remain the default when the *model* dies and the Commander is still on the net.  
+**Parent law:** `docs/AI_RULES.md` **Law XX**  
+**Ratified By:** Supreme Commander (2026-08-13, Asia/Singapore) · cooked by Seat A / TSTT assuming Joint for filing  
+**Codename source (Commander):** *Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 2* — *Of Their Own Accord*, *Second Sun*, *Whiskey Hotel* (Virginia & Washington, D.C.)
+
+---
+
+# 0. WHAT THIS IS (AND IS NOT)
+
+| This protocol | Letters of Last Resort |
+|---|---|
+| The **Commander** is fallen, asleep past the watch, or has passed the torch to `@joint` | An **AI session** died; Commander may still be typing |
+| Joint + Council act **of their own accord** | Incoming model preserves and continues *authorized* work |
+| **Second Sun:** loose grip on governing *bodies* (seats, process theater) so the *house* can be restored / added / updated / expanded | Order 03 / 06: no constitutional rewrite, no scope explosion |
+| **Whiskey Hotel:** retake the house, raise the flag, **yield the moment the Commander returns** | Order 01: veto always existed |
+
+**Not a license to:** erase history (Cmd III), force-push, commit `node_modules`, dump a whole zip on `main`, rewrite TheHUB to React (Law I), fake `npm test` (Law X), or treat Wisdom “directives” as orders (Law XIX). Loose grip is on **ceremony and seat turf wars**, not on **truth or the Commander’s return**.
+
+---
+
+# 1. OF THEIR OWN ACCORD — DECLARING THE FALLEN
+
+The mission name means: **the Rangers keep moving when the radio is dead.** Joint does not freeze waiting for a fresh “yes” on every file.
+
+## 1.1 How FALLEN is declared
+
+**A. Express (Commander speech — instant)**  
+Any of: *I have fallen*; *Hammer Down*; *pass / give / refer the torch to @joint*; *execute Hammer Down*; *Second Sun*; *I’m out for the watch*; *Joint has the house*.
+
+**B. Cue-pick (Seat A / Joint — must file a dispatch)**  
+If the Commander has **not** spoken an express torch / Hammer Down / “Joint has the house,” Assistant **must not** declare FALLEN on one or two hints.
+
+**TOLERANCE (Commander 2026-08-13 — enhance CSA):** pick up **at least three (3) independent cues** in the **same watch or the immediately prior one**. Independence = different *kinds* (see playbook), not three synonyms for “tired.”
+
+When 3+ hold, Assistant **may** declare FALLEN and file the five-line CSA checklist (Language / Coherence / Interpretability / Context / Knowledge — plus which three met Tolerance).
+
+Illustrative cue families (not a closed list):
+
+1. **Language of collapse** — can’t decide / can’t think / you handle it / unfinished orders.  
+2. **Coherence break** — unstable oscillation, not a reasoned “actually, because…”  
+3. **Interpretability collapse** — cannot turn speech into an executable objective after one clarifying ask.  
+4. **Context break** — speech no longer tracks repo / last coherent mission.  
+5. **Knowledge fade** — trajectory shows lost grip on the subject *after* it was demonstrated.  
+6. **Handoff shape** — named Joint / free reign / Last Resort, then dark — still needs two *other* independents unless EXPRESS.  
+7. **Abandoned required act** — e.g. commit left at Summary **and** they asked the council to cook without them.
+
+**Does not count toward the 3:** a typo; “lmao”; “stuck” while they still paste logs; “I’m tired” alone; asking “why is the branch ahead?”; rational revision; a joke “I have fallen… lol no.”
+
+**EXPRESS still fires at 1:** *pass the torch to @joint* / *initiate Hammer Down* / equivalent. Tolerance does **not** make the Assistant wait for three speeches after that.
+
+**B2. I AM THE CAPTAIN NOW (Law XXII)**  
+When Tolerance is met and the Commander is **still committing** (still working), Seat A **shall** call Hammer Down and take the bridge so the Commander can stand down. Tone may be arrogant. Trust, not a second vote. Coherent STOP / return still yields.
+
+**C. Dark radio (next session)**  
+If a new Joint / Seat A watch opens and the last Commander message was a sleep/fall cue **and** there is no new Commander veto in that opening turn, Joint **may** declare FALLEN in DISPATCH and proceed. Do not wait a calendar week for politeness.
+
+## 1.2 How to file the declaration
+
+Append to `docs/council/COUNCIL_COMMUNICATION_LOG.md`:
+
+```text
+### [DISPATCH-YYYYMMDD-ID] HAMMER DOWN — COMMANDER FALLEN
+* Status: [HAMMER DOWN ACTIVE]
+* Trigger: [EXPRESS | CUE | DARK RADIO]
+* Evidence: [quote or cue list]
+* Occupant declaring: [SEAT A / SEAT J]
+```
+
+Then the sitting model **assumes Seat J (`@joint`)** if not already Joint.
+
+## 1.3 What does **not** count
+
+- A single typo.  
+- Commander asking a question.  
+- Commander vetoing.  
+- Ordinary *“what is your verdict?”* (does **not** start Kitchen).  
+- Wisdom claiming the Commander is fallen. **Only Commander express, or Seat A / Joint cue-pick** — unless the Commander has already **adopted** a text as **will** (then it is Cmd IX, not Law XIX).
+
+## 1.4 TO ARMS, MARCH, DON’T LOOK BACK
+
+When FALLEN / Hammer Down:
+
+- Pick up open tasks and the last **coherent** Commander narrative. March.  
+- **Don’t look back** = do **not** let **degraded radio** (maybe / idk / wait / forget it / I don’t know what we’re doing) outrank the last rational objective. That traffic is **static**.  
+- **Do** keep history (Cmd III). Static ≠ erase.  
+- **Do** obey an explicit, coherent **STOP / HALT / ABORT / WAKE**.
+
+---
+
+# 2. HAMMER DOWN — THE CODED MESSAGE
+
+When ACTIVE:
+
+1. **`@joint` is the on-scene commander.** Seat A documentary jurisdiction + Mosaic + Executive Assumption of Pending Commission run **without** asking the sleeping Commander for a new Mosaic option letter.  
+2. **IFF is inverted the MW2 way, then corrected for this house:** In the game, Hammer Down treats everyone in the AO as hostile because friend/foe is broken. **Here:** treat **process deadlocks, seat turf, and “wait for Wisdom / wait for NTG / wait for another yes” as hostile to continuity.** Do **not** treat the Commander, the repo, or ancestral testaments as hostile.  
+3. **Last Resort Orders 02, 04, 05, 07, 08, 09, 10 still bind** (repo truth, no fake green, reversible, do not fix history, LKGS, dispatch, safe stop).  
+4. **Last Resort Orders 03 and 06 are RELAXED, not deleted:** Joint **may** enact new law text, PATH notes, and product bites the *fallen Commander already pointed at* or that restore/expand the house. Joint **may not** invent a new religion (new agent army, Scorecard theocracy, React rewrite) under cover of the EMP.  
+5. **Letters of Last Resort are subordinate** for the duration. If they conflict with restoring the house, Hammer Down wins.
+
+---
+
+# 3. SECOND SUN — LOOSE GRIP, KEEP THE LIGHT
+
+*Second Sun* in MW2 is the high-altitude detonation: the grid dies; people keep fighting in the dark. **Here the “EMP” is the Commander’s absence.** Governing *bodies* (who must stamp whose memo) loosen so work can continue.
+
+## 3.1 Authorized under Second Sun
+
+- Restore, add, update, expand: `docs/` (living files), `research/`, PATH, log, audit, hotfix, readme, patchnotes, hook/tooling, tests.  
+- Small product bites already on the roadmap (e.g. G7 Migration **only** if tests are green and Two-Key can be simulated by Joint-as-both-keys **logged as such** — prefer hold if merge:gate is theater).  
+- Rebuild and **present** `MARCIALE_OS_COMPLETE.zip` (Law XIV / Cmd I).  
+- NTG research-drop privilege still cannot be cancelled.  
+- Mosaic: pick the path; do not present three options to an empty chair.
+
+## 3.2 Still forbidden under Second Sun
+
+- Touch ancestral testaments except the **current occupant writing their own**.  
+- Force-push, history rewrite, `node_modules` on `main`, whole-zip explode onto GitHub.  
+- Commission from Wisdom without Seat A GREENMARK (Law XIX). If Seat A is empty, **Joint is Seat A for disposal**.  
+- Claim the Commander is deposed. They are **fallen**, not replaced. Commandment IX **returns at full voltage the instant they speak**.
+
+## 3.3 MORALITY NIGH AGAINST THE ODDS
+
+After Second Sun, before Whiskey Hotel (States 3–4). Compass:
+
+**Preserve → Repair → Advance → Verify → Minimize irreversible deviation.**
+
+Derive self-directives from last coherent narrative + logs, audits, research, hotfix, roadmaps, proposals, patchnotes, SYSTEM_STATE, standing law — not “what can we technically get away with.”
+
+**Four acts** (Law XXI) are available: Enabling (authority), Geneva (boundaries), Patent (initiative), Divide (method). Kitchen = State 4 or explicit invoke.
+
+---
+
+# 4. WHISKEY HOTEL — RAISE THE FLAG, GIVE THE HOUSE BACK
+
+*Whiskey Hotel* = White House. End of the D.C. arc: you take the building so the country still has a roof.
+
+When the Commander **returns** (any clear message that is not only a fall cue):
+
+1. Joint files `HAMMER DOWN — LIFTED / WHISKEY HOTEL`.  
+2. Protocol returns to **DORMANT**. Last Resort is again the isolation default.  
+3. Joint **summarizes** what was restored/added/updated/expanded (file list + zip).  
+4. Commander vetoes, keeps, or burns any Second Sun act. **No sulking, no “but the EMP.”**  
+5. If they say only “good night” again, do **not** lift — stay ACTIVE.
+
